kind i-want-to
title I want to use a font file that is installed but not active.
intro vtium treats a font file as missing until batch.conf lists it as active. `vtium-config activate` adds the file to the draft's active fonts, and the install writes batch.conf.
see fonts/try-a-font-set-whose-font-is-not-active

file etc/vtium.conf
    version = 1
    font-name = wide
    [head console]
    vt = 5
file etc/batch.conf
    ROOT/fonts/mono.bdf
font fonts/mono.bdf 8x16
font fonts/wide.bdf 10x20
frit wide
    source=bdf:ROOT/fonts/wide.bdf

at the start
# vtium treats wide.bdf as missing, so the console draws the built-in font.
check console font wide
check console fell-back yes
check console cell 8x16

1. Press q to quit.
2. Run `vtium-config activate ROOT/fonts/wide.bdf`.
3. Run `vtium-config install`.
at the install
check installed has "font-name = wide"
4. Restart vtium.
check console draws wide
check console cell 10x20
